# INTENTIONALLY EMPTY - no Pipeline is registered by this module.
#
# DataflowPipeline used to be listed here. It was removed in sprint-23
# (Story 1.2) for two independent reasons:
#
#  1. NOT CONSTRUCTIBLE. Its only constructor is
#     DataflowPipeline(String name, List<PipelineStage> stages)
#     (DataflowPipeline.java:72), so ServiceLoader raised
#     ServiceConfigurationError on every discovery pass. AutoConfig
#     swallowed that error before Story 1.1, so nothing ever said so.
#
#  2. A PIPELINE CANNOT SELF-CONFIGURE, EVEN IN PRINCIPLE. The Pipeline
#     contract IS a name plus a stage graph (Pipeline.java:18-21): the
#     stages are the pipeline's entire identity, not a setting attached to
#     it. No environment variable can supply a List<PipelineStage>, so
#     there is no honest no-arg constructor to write - a stand-in would
#     have to invent an empty or fake stage list, and DataflowPipeline
#     rejects an empty one by design (DataflowPipeline.java:78-80).
#
# AutoConfig.pipeline() (AutoConfig.java:256-258) therefore resolves empty
# on a GCP classpath. That is correct, not a gap: a pipeline is declared by
# the deployment that owns it, never discovered from the classpath.
#
# The class is unchanged and fully supported. Construct it explicitly:
#     new DataflowPipeline("my-pipeline", List.of(stageA, stageB))
